WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.239
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:29.509 --> 00:32.053
This man snuck into the castle town.

3
00:32.137 --> 00:33.304
And over and over,

4
00:33.888 --> 00:36.099
he stole food and valuables.

5
00:36.182 --> 00:37.350
A petty thief!

6
00:38.643 --> 00:41.312
What's worse, we found this in his possession.

7
00:44.107 --> 00:45.733
Yes, he's a ninja.

8
00:45.817 --> 00:49.821
He hid his name and background to inflict crime and violence upon us all.

9
00:53.700 --> 00:57.120
Thus, he is sentenced to death!

10
00:57.203 --> 00:58.413
Yes, sir!

11
01:00.707 --> 01:02.792
Get him!

12
01:02.876 --> 01:04.252
Get to it already…

13
01:04.335 --> 01:05.461
Kill him!

14
01:05.545 --> 01:07.005
Get him!

15
01:07.714 --> 01:09.257
Get to it already!

16
01:10.258 --> 01:11.551
This world is rotten,

17
01:12.886 --> 01:14.762
and I'm sick of living in it!

18
01:18.516 --> 01:19.893
SASUKE

19
01:19.976 --> 01:22.520
On second thought, I'm really sorry.

20
01:22.604 --> 01:25.106
-Kill him! Kill him! -Please, no!

21
01:32.655 --> 01:33.907
Just kidding!

22
01:33.990 --> 01:35.241
Oh, and I'm taking this.

23
01:37.744 --> 01:38.703
And this.

24
01:38.786 --> 01:40.663
Kill him! Now!

25
01:50.548 --> 01:54.302
After him! Don't let him escape! He must die!

26
02:14.614 --> 02:18.910
Please don't! I'm begging you! Spare me, please!

27
02:24.207 --> 02:27.961
I've got nothing against thieves, but you can't steal from a girl.

28
02:28.044 --> 02:29.045
Get him!

29
02:34.968 --> 02:36.010
Punk!

30
02:43.309 --> 02:44.185
Hey!

31
02:45.061 --> 02:46.020
Stop, or she dies!

32
02:54.112 --> 02:55.405
Good night.

33
02:59.242 --> 03:00.159
Sir…

34
03:01.411 --> 03:02.912
Thank you so much.

35
03:04.580 --> 03:06.290
If there's a girl in need of help,

36
03:07.458 --> 03:09.168
helping her is the obvious thing to do.

37
03:10.294 --> 03:13.047
OKUNI

38
03:13.673 --> 03:16.384
So, what do you say we get some dango at a teahouse?

39
03:17.885 --> 03:19.721
-Actually… -Do you dislike dango?

40
03:19.804 --> 03:21.097
No, that's not it.

41
03:31.733 --> 03:33.026
Ninja?

42
03:33.109 --> 03:35.820
That's as far as you go. Turn yourself in.

43
03:35.903 --> 03:39.824
You know, I just hate being ordered around.

44
03:42.994 --> 03:44.287
-Get ready to fly. -What?

45
04:22.658 --> 04:24.327
Not again.

46
04:25.703 --> 04:26.954
I'm Okuni.

47
04:27.830 --> 04:28.956
What's your name?

48
04:32.210 --> 04:33.211
Who, me?

49
04:34.462 --> 04:36.464
Neither moats nor castle walls mean anything to me.

50
04:37.256 --> 04:39.092
The best in the east, the ninja of flight.

51
04:39.717 --> 04:41.677
The name's Sasuke.

52
04:43.971 --> 04:45.890
So how about those dango?

53
04:47.266 --> 04:48.810
-Sure. -Really?

54
04:48.893 --> 04:49.852
It'd be my pleasure.

55
04:50.895 --> 04:52.230
Hooray!

56
04:58.653 --> 05:01.114
These guys are so persistent.

57
05:01.781 --> 05:02.865
Let's go!

58
05:08.329 --> 05:09.455
Poison…

59
05:12.875 --> 05:14.168
Are you all right?

60
05:14.252 --> 05:15.253
Run.

61
05:16.045 --> 05:17.004
Yes.

62
05:41.195 --> 05:43.990
Shield, Sanctuary, Strike, Flame Release!

63
05:44.073 --> 05:45.199
FLAME RELEASE

64
06:24.488 --> 06:25.823
My rice balls

65
06:26.449 --> 06:28.034
are delicious, you know.

66
06:44.217 --> 06:45.176
He's awake!

67
06:45.259 --> 06:46.552
Master Hakuunsai!

68
06:49.597 --> 06:51.557
It's been five years, Sasuke.

69
06:51.641 --> 06:52.475
HAKUUNSAI

70
06:52.558 --> 06:53.768
Old man.

71
06:54.435 --> 06:57.313
You've sunk so low you've become a bandit.

72
06:58.314 --> 06:59.815
You just had to stick your nose in.

73
07:00.316 --> 07:01.734
What are you trying to pull?

74
07:02.401 --> 07:03.569
I thought

75
07:04.445 --> 07:05.947
I'd knock some sense into you.

76
07:06.447 --> 07:08.908
How I live my life is my business.

77
07:08.991 --> 07:11.536
-Here. Eat up. -No, thanks.

78
07:13.829 --> 07:16.541
Your pickled plums are too sour.

79
07:16.624 --> 07:18.417
Grandpa, it's time to train.

80
07:18.501 --> 07:19.794
Coming.

81
07:20.378 --> 07:22.713
-Wanna join us, mister? -"Mister"?

82
07:23.297 --> 07:24.507
Who's this brat?

83
07:24.590 --> 07:25.883
Kids just like you.

84
07:27.051 --> 07:28.803
They're all orphans.

85
07:30.137 --> 07:32.515
Are you still doing this?

86
07:32.598 --> 07:33.891
Even though you're broke?

87
07:35.518 --> 07:38.938
And you're still using those beat-up shuriken?

88
07:40.690 --> 07:44.360
Listen. You'll never get strong staying in a dump like this.

89
07:47.655 --> 07:50.449
Do yourself a favor and get out while you can.

90
07:52.451 --> 07:54.287
Well, I'm off.

91
07:55.079 --> 07:56.247
Wait.

92
07:57.248 --> 07:59.333
Not until you beat me.

93
07:59.417 --> 08:01.544
Don't push yourself, old man.

94
08:01.627 --> 08:04.088
There's no way I'd lose to a mere thief.

95
08:05.256 --> 08:08.676
What's the difference between a thief and a ninja?

96
08:10.094 --> 08:12.221
A ninja who serves no lord

97
08:13.139 --> 08:14.765
is just a thief.

98
08:16.517 --> 08:18.519
You're the only one

99
08:19.437 --> 08:20.521
saying that bullshit!

100
08:35.494 --> 08:37.538
I'd rather die

101
08:38.247 --> 08:40.041
than live bowing to anyone!

102
08:43.252 --> 08:45.212
No matter how hard I train…

103
08:47.048 --> 08:49.258
or how much I hone my skills,

104
08:50.843 --> 08:52.637
people still look down on us

105
08:53.846 --> 08:55.181
and mock us

106
08:55.931 --> 08:57.308
just for being ninjas!

107
09:00.853 --> 09:02.772
I'll use my power

108
09:03.898 --> 09:05.858
to live as I please

109
09:05.941 --> 09:08.361
and take whatever I want!

110
09:16.369 --> 09:17.370
Your strength

111
09:18.621 --> 09:21.832
is meant to serve others.

112
09:23.334 --> 09:24.460
Others?

113
09:25.670 --> 09:28.547
What have they ever done for me?

114
09:35.971 --> 09:38.599
You've grown old, Hakuunsai.

115
09:38.683 --> 09:42.228
Is bowing your head really so unbearable?

116
09:50.778 --> 09:52.738
Conceal, Secure, Bind, Switch!

117
09:52.822 --> 09:53.823
SWITCH

118
09:57.910 --> 09:59.412
-Body Switch! -Body Switch!

119
10:01.747 --> 10:03.833
So you finally bowed your head.

120
10:03.916 --> 10:05.418
Damn it…

121
10:06.711 --> 10:08.170
Sasuke.

122
10:08.963 --> 10:10.756
Even in a world like this,

123
10:12.842 --> 10:14.593
there are still good people.

124
10:22.601 --> 10:24.854
Still can't keep your hands to yourself, huh?

125
10:25.771 --> 10:27.106
It's probably cheap junk, anyway.

126
10:28.107 --> 10:29.692
This sword…

127
10:34.905 --> 10:37.032
is the cursed blade Muramasa.

128
10:38.200 --> 10:39.201
A cursed blade?

129
10:40.327 --> 10:45.082
It's said to bring misfortune to Tokugawa Ieyasu and his clan.

130
10:46.083 --> 10:46.959
That's why

131
10:47.543 --> 10:51.589
it's considered a protective blade by those who oppose the Tokugawa.

132
10:52.882 --> 10:54.800
Lord Sanada Masayuki gave it to me

133
10:55.342 --> 10:58.012
as a reward for the Battle of Ueda.

134
10:58.554 --> 11:00.181
The Battle of Ueda?

135
11:01.599 --> 11:02.641
Sanada?

136
11:03.934 --> 11:06.896
You don't know? The legendary Sanada clan and their Ten Braves.

137
11:07.521 --> 11:08.522
What?

138
11:09.190 --> 11:10.191
Well, then…

139
11:11.233 --> 11:12.860
The year is 1600.

140
11:13.527 --> 11:14.987
Fourteen years ago,

141
11:15.905 --> 11:18.949
a great battle was fought that would divide Japan into two.

142
11:19.033 --> 11:20.201
TOKUGAWA ARMY - SANADA ARMY

143
11:20.284 --> 11:23.120
Against the Eastern Army led by Tokugawa Ieyasu,

144
11:23.204 --> 11:26.332
the Sanada clan barricaded themselves inside Ueda Castle in Shinano Province,

145
11:27.041 --> 11:30.044
where they faced the forces of Hidetada, Ieyasu's eldest son,

146
11:30.711 --> 11:33.297
as he marched to the decisive Battle of Sekigahara.

147
11:34.006 --> 11:35.799
Their forces outnumbered the Sanada, 20 to 1.

148
11:36.509 --> 11:39.428
Hidetada was certain of victory,

149
11:39.512 --> 11:43.307
but Lord Sanada Masayuki was lying in wait.

150
11:43.390 --> 11:44.266
HAKUUNSAI

151
11:45.434 --> 11:48.437
A sudden flood swept away Hidetada's troops,

152
11:49.647 --> 11:53.484
then Masayuki's son, Lord Nobushige, launched a surprise attack.

153
11:53.567 --> 11:54.693
SANADA NOBUSHIGE

154
11:54.777 --> 12:00.324
Next, a mighty arrow from master archer Unno Rokuro pierced the enemy ranks,

155
12:00.407 --> 12:02.368
throwing Hidetada's army into chaos.

156
12:02.993 --> 12:04.995
As a thick fog shrouded the battlefield,

157
12:05.621 --> 12:07.831
the Sanada Braves,

158
12:07.915 --> 12:11.126
masters of ninjutsu and martial arts, struck one after another.

159
12:11.877 --> 12:14.755
The young genius, Kirigakure Saizo.

160
12:15.422 --> 12:18.425
Master of the chain-sickle, Yuri Kamanosuke.

161
12:20.719 --> 12:22.763
The strongman, Miyoshi Isa.

162
12:24.473 --> 12:27.059
The poison expert, Miyoshi Seikai.

163
12:29.103 --> 12:31.939
The loyal warrior, Mochizuki Rokuro.

164
12:32.898 --> 12:35.401
The strategist, Anayama Kosuke.

165
12:36.318 --> 12:39.905
The ninja of a hundred skills, Nezu Jinpachi.

166
12:40.823 --> 12:43.492
Through the cunning of Sanada Masayuki and Nobushige,

167
12:43.576 --> 12:46.829
and the brave warriors' fierce resistance, Hidetada's army was routed.

168
12:47.830 --> 12:49.373
They never made it

169
12:50.207 --> 12:53.752
to the decisive Battle of Sekigahara in time.

170
12:55.379 --> 12:57.631
Despite the Sanada clan's valiant efforts,

171
12:58.340 --> 13:01.594
the Tokugawa emerged victorious.

172
13:02.469 --> 13:03.345
But…

173
13:04.013 --> 13:07.391
-You disgrace us! -…Ieyasu's fury was said to be immense.

174
13:07.474 --> 13:08.434
Father.

175
13:09.310 --> 13:10.728
Forgive me!

176
13:10.811 --> 13:11.937
Damn it…

177
13:12.021 --> 13:12.896
TOKUGAWA IEYASU

178
13:12.980 --> 13:14.398
Those Sanada!

179
13:14.481 --> 13:16.817
The Tokugawa had lost to the Sanada before.

180
13:16.900 --> 13:18.736
This was their second humiliation.

181
13:19.320 --> 13:21.822
-And so, having incurred… -I'll curse them for all eternity!

182
13:21.905 --> 13:24.658
…Ieyasu's wrath, Lord Masayuki and Lord Nobushige

183
13:25.284 --> 13:26.744
were ordered into confinement

184
13:27.328 --> 13:30.456
and placed under strict surveillance.

185
13:31.290 --> 13:32.458
What a load of crap.

186
13:33.584 --> 13:34.960
The Sanada Braves?

187
13:35.836 --> 13:38.255
I doubt guys that strong ever existed.

188
13:38.339 --> 13:40.299
They were strong indeed.

189
13:41.175 --> 13:43.719
Far stronger than you'll ever be.

190
13:44.928 --> 13:48.182
Because they fought out of loyalty to their lord.

191
13:51.769 --> 13:53.354
You can have this sword.

192
13:55.648 --> 13:56.482
Come on!

193
13:56.565 --> 13:57.858
Let's eat.

194
13:58.734 --> 13:59.818
You're hungry, aren't you?

195
14:01.820 --> 14:02.863
Not really.

196
14:06.200 --> 14:08.702
I can tell when you're lying.

197
14:11.997 --> 14:13.248
Got anywhere to go back to?

198
14:17.836 --> 14:20.214
Look, I made it so well!

199
14:20.297 --> 14:22.549
-That's very good. -What's that?

200
14:22.633 --> 14:24.593
-Plum. -Oh, plum.

201
14:38.691 --> 14:39.650
Hey, Grandpa.

202
14:40.317 --> 14:42.695
What happened to Lord Sanada after that?

203
14:42.778 --> 14:43.988
Who knows?

204
14:45.114 --> 14:46.824
I wonder how he's doing.

205
14:59.920 --> 15:01.338
You've had too much to drink.

206
15:01.422 --> 15:04.091
KUDOYAMA VILLAGE

207
15:05.509 --> 15:06.593
What brings you here?

208
15:07.594 --> 15:10.305
I've come to pay my respects to Lord Sanada Masayuki.

209
15:10.389 --> 15:12.182
KUDOYAMA VILLAGE TRAVEL PASS

210
15:12.266 --> 15:14.351
THIS PERSON IS AUTHORIZED TO TRAVEL WITHOUT HINDRANCE

211
15:14.435 --> 15:15.686
All right. You can pass.

212
15:33.370 --> 15:34.204
Wait!

213
15:44.298 --> 15:45.674
SHUTO KAGEAKI

214
15:45.758 --> 15:46.759
Go.

215
16:39.103 --> 16:40.104
Father.

216
16:40.938 --> 16:43.690
The pickled plums turned out delicious again this year.

217
16:49.613 --> 16:55.536
Even after defeating Ieyasu twice…

218
17:03.627 --> 17:05.003
This bitter regret…

219
17:06.130 --> 17:08.966
You must avenge me.

220
17:11.260 --> 17:12.261
Father.

221
17:26.066 --> 17:29.153
SANADA YUKIMURA

222
17:29.236 --> 17:30.529
My lord.

223
17:31.196 --> 17:34.533
A traveling monk has come to pay his respects.

224
17:34.616 --> 17:37.911
I am Sojun, a monk traveling across the land.

225
17:37.995 --> 17:41.123
You must be Lord Nobushige.

226
17:41.832 --> 17:43.834
I go by Yukimura now.

227
17:45.043 --> 17:47.671
You've taken the "Yuki" from your father's name.

228
17:48.297 --> 17:49.131
Yes.

229
17:51.049 --> 17:52.968
I've come on behalf of the Toyotomi.

230
17:53.051 --> 17:54.094
The Toyotomi?!

231
17:54.678 --> 17:55.888
This is my son, Daisuke.

232
17:57.681 --> 17:58.682
I see.

233
17:59.308 --> 18:00.350
And?

234
18:01.894 --> 18:03.520
Ieyasu has finally declared his intent

235
18:04.146 --> 18:06.440
to destroy the Toyotomi.

236
18:09.109 --> 18:10.068
Please take a look.

237
18:14.823 --> 18:16.700
This is the inscription on the bell

238
18:17.367 --> 18:21.288
dedicated by Lord Hideyori and Lady Yodo upon the reconstruction of Hokoji Temple.

239
18:21.371 --> 18:22.456
MAY THE NATION BE PEACEFUL

240
18:23.916 --> 18:25.792
It means the realm will be at peace,

241
18:25.876 --> 18:29.546
and everyone from the ruler to the common people

242
18:30.214 --> 18:32.132
will live in prosperity and happiness.

243
18:33.383 --> 18:35.135
But Lord Ieyasu interpreted it

244
18:36.303 --> 18:38.555
as splitting his name in two

245
18:38.639 --> 18:41.892
and proclaiming the Toyotomi as the rightful rulers.

246
18:42.893 --> 18:45.437
So he took it as an insult to the Tokugawa?

247
18:45.562 --> 18:49.107
Yes. He was absolutely furious.

248
18:51.735 --> 18:54.821
The Toyotomi need your strength now more than ever, Lord Yukimura.

249
18:54.905 --> 18:59.910
Please, return to Osaka for the sake of the Toyotomi clan.

250
19:03.538 --> 19:06.959
Lady Yodo sent me a letter as well, asking me to come to her aid.

251
19:08.043 --> 19:08.877
Then…

252
19:09.461 --> 19:10.712
I'm afraid I must refuse.

253
19:11.797 --> 19:13.674
I've been confined here for 14 years.

254
19:14.258 --> 19:16.969
I no longer have the strength to wage war.

255
19:17.052 --> 19:20.597
What about the braves who fought at the Battle of Ueda?

256
19:21.306 --> 19:23.308
They've all left my side.

257
19:24.601 --> 19:25.602
As you can see,

258
19:26.311 --> 19:28.480
only my son, Daisuke, remains.

259
19:29.773 --> 19:32.693
I've even sent my wife back to our home province.

260
19:34.778 --> 19:37.572
I can never leave this village alive.

261
19:39.199 --> 19:42.244
Will you really waste away in these mountains?

262
19:42.327 --> 19:46.540
You, the son of Lord Sanada Masayuki, who defeated Tokugawa Ieyasu twice?

263
19:47.416 --> 19:48.750
Life here…

264
19:50.502 --> 19:51.795
isn't so bad.

265
20:12.441 --> 20:13.442
I wonder

266
20:14.359 --> 20:16.570
what's happening out there in the world.

267
20:17.446 --> 20:21.199
If you command me to, I'll find out whether his story is true.

268
20:21.283 --> 20:23.327
KIRIGAKURE SAIZO

269
20:23.410 --> 20:24.703
No, leave it.

270
20:25.996 --> 20:27.998
I'm sorry, Saizo.

271
20:31.293 --> 20:32.669
Kill her!

272
20:33.211 --> 20:34.254
Please wait!

273
20:34.338 --> 20:35.464
What's going on?

274
20:36.673 --> 20:39.051
That woman was hiding rice

275
20:39.718 --> 20:41.887
to avoid paying her taxes.

276
20:41.970 --> 20:43.096
Get on with it!

277
20:43.180 --> 20:47.351
Would Lord Ieyasu really approve of killing a peasant?

278
20:47.434 --> 20:48.810
Then as punishment,

279
20:49.519 --> 20:52.397
I'll raise this village's taxes by 30%.

280
20:53.231 --> 20:56.068
-But… -Please. Just endure it for now.

281
20:56.151 --> 20:58.695
You can't even leave this village.

282
21:00.238 --> 21:01.948
What else can you do?

283
21:02.908 --> 21:04.284
This should be fun.

284
21:05.952 --> 21:06.995
Let's go!

285
21:08.538 --> 21:10.457
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

286
21:11.416 --> 21:15.295
If it weren't for you, we'd be free to come and go from the village.

287
21:16.713 --> 21:17.798
I'm sorry.

288
21:28.058 --> 21:31.686
-Damn it! Lost again. -I'm on a lucky streak today.

289
21:31.770 --> 21:32.813
Here you go.

290
21:32.896 --> 21:34.689
YURI KAMANOSUKE

291
21:34.773 --> 21:38.110
MIYOSHI SEIKAI

292
21:41.947 --> 21:44.825
NEZU JINPACHI

293
21:45.409 --> 21:48.120
UNNO ROKURO

294
21:50.622 --> 21:54.251
Everyone's suffering, and this is what we're stuck doing?

295
21:58.171 --> 21:59.923
MIYOSHI ISA

296
22:00.006 --> 22:01.007
Unno.

297
22:01.550 --> 22:04.886
I know how you feel, but we have to endure it for now.

298
22:04.970 --> 22:05.804
MOCHIZUKI ROKURO

299
22:05.887 --> 22:07.806
If our true identities are discovered…

300
22:07.889 --> 22:08.723
ANAYAMA KOSUKE

301
22:08.807 --> 22:10.976
…it'll be the end of the Sanada clan and this village.

302
22:12.936 --> 22:15.480
We've been told to endure it for 14 years.

303
22:17.023 --> 22:20.318
Hey, Mochizuki, you've really turned into an old man.

304
22:20.402 --> 22:21.820
You haven't forgotten, have you?

305
22:22.571 --> 22:24.406
This is just a disguise.

306
22:27.117 --> 22:28.368
Hey! Are you listening, Isa?

307
22:30.162 --> 22:31.204
What?

308
22:34.708 --> 22:36.751
Think Lord Yukimura's holding up, too?

309
22:37.586 --> 22:39.379
He hasn't really gone soft, has he?

310
22:39.963 --> 22:41.131
Trust our lord.

311
22:42.799 --> 22:44.885
Haven't we always done that?

312
22:58.190 --> 23:00.692
TOKUGAWA HIDETADA

313
23:39.731 --> 23:40.649
You're back.

314
23:42.025 --> 23:42.943
Yes, my lord.

315
23:45.153 --> 23:46.112
What of the Sanada?

316
23:47.822 --> 23:49.950
Their fangs are gone.

317
23:50.033 --> 23:52.410
They're living like old men.

318
23:52.494 --> 23:54.246
I see, I see.

319
23:55.205 --> 23:56.748
Without his retainers,

320
23:57.666 --> 23:59.459
even a Sanada is just an ordinary man.

321
24:00.043 --> 24:00.919
My lord,

322
24:01.002 --> 24:04.422
that scheme with Hokoji Temple was brilliant.

323
24:04.506 --> 24:07.467
That was Suden's scheme.

324
24:07.592 --> 24:12.222
As expected of Lord Konchiin, the Tokugawa's brains.

325
24:13.098 --> 24:14.140
Well…

326
24:14.808 --> 24:17.936
It was all thanks to the Great Shogun's wisdom

327
24:18.019 --> 24:20.605
in heeding my humble counsel.

328
24:20.689 --> 24:21.648
KONCHIIN SUDEN

329
24:26.194 --> 24:27.988
Sojun. Come closer.

330
24:28.780 --> 24:29.739
Yes, my lord.

331
24:30.740 --> 24:32.367
Your promised reward.

332
24:33.285 --> 24:35.245
The fabled elixir.

333
24:35.328 --> 24:37.247
Savor its power.

334
24:38.707 --> 24:40.041
I'm deeply grateful.

335
24:47.882 --> 24:49.718
I can feel the power surging within me.

336
24:50.635 --> 24:51.720
Good, good.

337
24:52.554 --> 24:53.972
However, Great Shogun,

338
24:54.764 --> 24:56.474
if he's a concern,

339
24:56.558 --> 24:58.810
why not simply kill him?

340
25:00.020 --> 25:04.566
But then, it would all end there.

341
25:10.739 --> 25:11.948
Take his land,

342
25:13.533 --> 25:14.743
strip him of his power,

343
25:15.910 --> 25:17.579
and let him do nothing

344
25:17.662 --> 25:18.955
but grow old.

345
25:21.166 --> 25:22.375
For a samurai,

346
25:23.209 --> 25:26.421
that is the most humiliating punishment of all.

347
25:31.718 --> 25:32.844
So it failed.

348
25:32.927 --> 25:35.722
Let's lower the dose of poison nut next time.

349
25:36.723 --> 25:37.766
Right.

350
25:43.730 --> 25:45.440
Where did he go?

351
25:45.523 --> 25:47.984
There he is! The thief!

352
25:51.321 --> 25:52.947
What a haul!

353
25:55.033 --> 25:56.951
Kagemaru! Kill him!

354
25:58.453 --> 25:59.412
Kagemaru?!

355
26:00.288 --> 26:01.289
Sasuke?

356
26:05.251 --> 26:09.172
You used to be a village thug. How'd you end up as a bodyguard?

357
26:11.674 --> 26:13.134
I gave up stealing.

358
26:14.177 --> 26:15.762
-What? -Not only that.

359
26:16.763 --> 26:18.515
My fighting skills were recognized,

360
26:19.432 --> 26:21.267
and now I serve Lord Tokugawa.

361
26:22.477 --> 26:24.896
Tokugawa… You mean the Tokugawa clan?

362
26:25.522 --> 26:26.689
That's right.

363
26:26.773 --> 26:29.401
They're hiring lots of ninjas now.

364
26:31.027 --> 26:33.947
The Tokugawa will rule Japan from now on.

365
26:35.281 --> 26:36.866
My mom's so proud of me.

366
26:38.701 --> 26:42.455
You should quit this nonsense and get an honest job.

367
26:43.164 --> 26:44.416
Make your parents proud.

368
26:45.834 --> 26:47.961
I don't have any parents.

369
26:50.338 --> 26:51.756
Old man Hakuunsai…

370
26:52.549 --> 26:54.175
He's been looking for you all this time.

371
27:01.641 --> 27:02.851
He's getting old, after all.

372
27:04.436 --> 27:06.563
He's probably planning to leave the kids in your care.

373
27:12.152 --> 27:13.653
I'm taking this back.

374
27:18.241 --> 27:20.076
What's that pouch in your pocket?

375
27:22.745 --> 27:23.580
Well…

376
27:25.665 --> 27:26.958
It's the old man's.

377
27:28.334 --> 27:29.794
Come on.

378
27:29.878 --> 27:32.255
There's probably nothing valuable in it, anyway.

379
27:41.139 --> 27:43.475
BOW BEFORE WHAT IS RIGHT AND CURB YOUR PRIDE

380
27:43.558 --> 27:47.979
"Use your power for the good of all."

381
28:22.138 --> 28:23.806
Look, you messed up again. You suck.

382
28:23.890 --> 28:25.725
Just one more time! Just one more!

383
28:25.808 --> 28:27.769
-Let me have a turn. -Please!

384
28:29.812 --> 28:31.147
-Amazing! -Amazing!

385
28:32.440 --> 28:33.733
-Sasuke! -Sasuke!

386
28:34.817 --> 28:37.862
Hey. Are you guys training properly?

387
28:38.947 --> 28:41.324
Guess I'll have to step in and coach you.

388
28:49.374 --> 28:51.417
You're back, Sasuke?

389
28:57.423 --> 28:58.716
So you're Hakuunsai.

390
29:04.055 --> 29:05.431
Serve the Tokugawa.

391
29:05.515 --> 29:06.474
HATTORI HANZO

392
29:07.308 --> 29:08.268
Hattori…

393
29:10.311 --> 29:11.271
Hanzo.

394
29:24.200 --> 29:25.118
Old man!

395
29:25.201 --> 29:26.369
What the hell?!

396
29:26.452 --> 29:28.204
Sasuke, run…

397
29:29.581 --> 29:31.374
Take the children!

398
29:32.083 --> 29:33.001
You there.

399
29:33.585 --> 29:36.337
You're the thief who escaped the execution grounds.

400
29:37.380 --> 29:39.299
Thanks to you, I found his whereabouts.

401
29:40.008 --> 29:41.009
I owe you one.

402
29:41.593 --> 29:43.511
You bastard!

403
29:46.806 --> 29:48.683
Lord Hakuunsai!

404
29:52.562 --> 29:57.692
Conceal, Secure, Bind, Switch!

405
30:02.614 --> 30:03.531
Old man!

406
30:10.413 --> 30:11.247
Old man!

407
30:13.124 --> 30:15.585
You bastard…

408
30:16.878 --> 30:19.339
I'll make you pay!

409
30:30.308 --> 30:31.225
Old man.

410
30:34.020 --> 30:35.021
That technique

411
30:35.688 --> 30:36.689
just now…

412
30:37.732 --> 30:38.775
I don't know.

413
30:46.157 --> 30:47.367
It was…

414
30:48.660 --> 30:49.702
Clone.

415
30:58.544 --> 30:59.545
Sasuke…

416
31:01.005 --> 31:01.965
What?

417
31:12.266 --> 31:13.351
Go to…

418
31:14.268 --> 31:15.103
Kudoyama.

419
31:16.813 --> 31:17.730
Kudoyama?

420
31:24.779 --> 31:25.863
There…

421
31:26.823 --> 31:28.074
There…

422
31:40.920 --> 31:41.921
Hey…

423
31:43.131 --> 31:44.132
Hey, old man!

424
31:45.299 --> 31:46.551
Old man!

425
31:46.634 --> 31:49.470
Hang in there, old man! Hey!

426
31:50.179 --> 31:51.305
Hey!

427
31:54.350 --> 31:56.894
What did the old man ever do to you?!

428
31:57.854 --> 31:58.771
Hey!

429
32:04.902 --> 32:07.030
You bastard…

430
32:09.949 --> 32:10.783
Enchain.

431
32:10.867 --> 32:11.701
ENCHAIN

432
32:15.580 --> 32:17.540
You want to know what he did?

433
32:19.375 --> 32:20.460
I'll tell you.

434
32:22.295 --> 32:25.506
He rejected the Great Elder's generous offer,

435
32:27.508 --> 32:29.093
and chose the Sanada instead.

436
32:34.182 --> 32:36.601
All for some foolish loyalty.

437
32:44.358 --> 32:47.487
Ninjas are the source of the Tokugawa's power!

438
32:48.738 --> 32:51.699
You will support this nation from the shadows!

439
32:52.492 --> 32:53.534
Yes, sir!

440
32:53.618 --> 32:55.620
Simply obey your orders.

441
32:56.370 --> 32:57.622
Yes, sir!

442
32:57.705 --> 32:58.748
Jump!

443
33:00.583 --> 33:02.460
I said jump.

444
33:21.229 --> 33:22.146
Mom…

445
33:24.023 --> 33:24.857
Mom…

446
33:25.483 --> 33:26.484
I'm sorry!

447
33:42.250 --> 33:43.918
Not a single one left, eh?

448
33:49.757 --> 33:52.343
Not even a ninja who can fly?

449
33:54.387 --> 33:55.721
A flying ninja…

450
33:56.889 --> 33:57.932
How marvelous.

451
34:03.312 --> 34:04.438
What of Hakuunsai?

452
34:06.649 --> 34:07.692
I cut him down.

453
34:08.276 --> 34:09.443
I see.

454
34:11.612 --> 34:13.531
Yukimura and Hakuunsai…

455
34:14.991 --> 34:17.535
Now we have nothing to fear from behind us.

456
34:55.239 --> 34:56.574
It's all my fault.

457
35:18.429 --> 35:20.014
Kudoyama…

458
35:23.809 --> 35:24.894
Okuni!

459
35:25.811 --> 35:28.272
-You're back, Okuni. -Sorry to keep you waiting.

460
35:28.898 --> 35:30.191
Well? How did it go?

461
35:30.274 --> 35:32.443
I was sure this batch would sell well.

462
35:32.526 --> 35:34.487
As you can see, they're all sold out.

463
35:35.571 --> 35:39.408
The unbreakable Sanada cords are gaining fame across the land.

464
35:40.368 --> 35:42.578
Here's the payment, and what you asked for.

465
35:43.246 --> 35:44.372
This is a great help.

466
35:47.291 --> 35:48.125
All right.

467
35:52.672 --> 35:53.839
That's a lot.

468
35:53.923 --> 35:55.800
This should keep us fed for a while.

469
35:56.384 --> 35:57.885
We're deeply grateful!

470
35:58.844 --> 35:59.804
Thank Okuni.

471
36:00.429 --> 36:03.641
The Sanada cord has become fairly well-known by now.

472
36:04.976 --> 36:06.394
I'll teach everyone how to make it.

473
36:07.144 --> 36:08.813
I hope it'll help you all make a living.

474
36:09.522 --> 36:11.565
Lord Yukimura, let's play tag!

475
36:11.649 --> 36:12.858
Let's play tag!

476
36:12.942 --> 36:13.943
All right.

477
36:15.903 --> 36:17.780
No matter how dire the situation,

478
36:17.863 --> 36:19.615
there's always a way to turn things around.

479
36:20.658 --> 36:24.245
But… how do you manage to weave so many cords?

480
36:29.625 --> 36:30.626
As expected of our lord.

481
36:31.752 --> 36:33.504
Well? What do you think, Unno?

482
36:34.588 --> 36:37.842
I'll have you know I never doubted our lord for a second.

483
36:39.093 --> 36:42.972
And who was it that said he'd gone soft?

484
36:43.055 --> 36:45.057
I was just venting!

485
36:46.017 --> 36:49.061
It's paid off, all the hard work we've put into improving the Sanada cords.

486
36:49.645 --> 36:52.315
Well, my brother did most of the work.

487
36:53.024 --> 36:55.901
All right! Number 2053.

488
36:59.071 --> 37:00.281
That's enough!

489
37:01.032 --> 37:03.909
What are you lot doing? Hey!

490
37:04.910 --> 37:07.121
What's all this money?!

491
37:07.788 --> 37:10.041
I have good news for you.

492
37:10.833 --> 37:15.629
The rice allowance granted to the Sanada by the Great Elder

493
37:17.256 --> 37:19.258
will be cut by half starting next season.

494
37:20.134 --> 37:24.722
"Keep the common folk alive, but not well enough to live."

495
37:25.639 --> 37:27.391
Those are the Great Elder's orders.

496
37:28.559 --> 37:30.144
The common folk!

497
37:30.811 --> 37:34.482
Keep them alive, but not well enough to live.

498
37:34.565 --> 37:35.566
Bastards…

499
37:44.950 --> 37:46.911
It's all thanks to you. Have a drink.

500
37:53.834 --> 37:56.295
If we're going to deal with him, let me do it.

501
37:56.379 --> 38:00.049
-No, poison would be more certain. -Don't act rashly!

502
38:00.132 --> 38:03.302
If the checkpoint magistrate dies, Lord Yukimura will be the prime suspect.

503
38:04.970 --> 38:08.182
But if they cut our rice allowance any further…

504
38:08.265 --> 38:10.226
Don't worry about me.

505
38:10.726 --> 38:12.144
Even so…

506
38:12.228 --> 38:14.939
You've been giving rice to the poor villagers,

507
38:15.022 --> 38:17.358
and you're barely eating yourself, aren't you?

508
38:17.441 --> 38:19.151
My presence…

509
38:19.777 --> 38:22.279
is a burden on this village.

510
38:23.614 --> 38:24.740
That's the least I could do.

511
38:24.824 --> 38:26.367
We'll have to leave the village, then.

512
38:27.410 --> 38:29.161
There must be a way if we just try.

513
38:30.121 --> 38:32.039
Have you forgotten about that thief

514
38:32.665 --> 38:35.668
who came to this village the other day?

515
38:52.852 --> 38:54.353
But if things go on like this…

516
38:57.189 --> 38:58.482
We're still missing…

517
39:00.234 --> 39:01.318
one last piece.

518
39:22.631 --> 39:25.050
Botched the landing again.

519
39:28.929 --> 39:31.015
So this is Kudoyama, huh?

520
39:35.936 --> 39:36.896
Hey, you.

521
39:38.898 --> 39:40.816
Recognize this shuriken?

522
39:47.907 --> 39:48.824
Are you all right?

523
39:49.742 --> 39:50.576
Yeah.

524
39:55.915 --> 39:57.333
It's the same design.

525
40:01.045 --> 40:02.421
So it was you lot!

526
40:17.645 --> 40:18.854
You're as good as Saizo.

527
40:28.113 --> 40:31.242
You're the ones who killed the old man!

528
40:40.042 --> 40:43.170
Shield, Secure, Surge…

529
40:45.422 --> 40:46.924
Mist Concealment.

530
40:47.007 --> 40:48.133
MIST CONCEALMENT

531
41:09.321 --> 41:12.491
BOMB

532
41:13.075 --> 41:14.243
Let go of me.

533
41:24.795 --> 41:27.506
-Are you all in cahoots? -Yeah.

534
41:29.675 --> 41:30.718
Looking for this?

535
41:31.760 --> 41:33.762
I took it for safekeeping. It's dangerous.

536
41:34.513 --> 41:36.932
What kind of behavior is that, attacking us out of nowhere?

537
41:37.016 --> 41:39.393
What ninja clan are you from?

538
41:39.476 --> 41:41.353
Now that you've seen us, we have to kill you.

539
41:41.437 --> 41:42.438
Shall we?

540
41:44.315 --> 41:45.524
Double sixes.

541
41:45.608 --> 41:47.318
Now that's a roll.

542
41:47.401 --> 41:49.028
Then let's proceed at once.

543
41:49.111 --> 41:50.112
Wait.

544
42:01.248 --> 42:02.416
Where did you get this?

545
42:05.044 --> 42:06.003
It's a keepsake.

546
42:06.629 --> 42:07.963
From the old man who died.

547
42:09.256 --> 42:10.341
Was this old man…

548
42:11.175 --> 42:12.760
Hakuunsai?

549
42:14.219 --> 42:15.179
Yeah.

550
42:16.347 --> 42:17.431
I see.

551
42:18.515 --> 42:19.850
So he's passed away.

552
42:21.769 --> 42:22.686
What's your name?

553
42:23.896 --> 42:25.022
Sasuke.

554
42:25.898 --> 42:27.733
I'm sorry we treated you so roughly.

555
42:27.816 --> 42:30.361
Everyone, put away your weapons.

556
42:30.444 --> 42:31.445
Yes, sir.

557
42:36.241 --> 42:37.951
I'm Sanada Yukimura.

558
42:39.078 --> 42:41.372
I knew Hakuunsai well.

559
42:41.455 --> 42:42.581
Sanada?

560
42:45.834 --> 42:48.879
So you're the famous Sanada Braves?

561
42:50.506 --> 42:53.050
You're nothing like what I'd heard.

562
42:53.133 --> 42:54.927
What do you mean by that?

563
42:56.261 --> 43:00.099
Then why are you using the same shuriken as the ninja who killed the old man?

564
43:00.766 --> 43:02.184
Acting all high and mighty.

565
43:03.894 --> 43:06.438
The one who killed Hakuunsai was most likely…

566
43:09.191 --> 43:10.401
Hattori Hanzo.

567
43:12.236 --> 43:13.529
Hattori Hanzo?

568
43:13.612 --> 43:17.574
The head ninja of the Tokugawa clan. The greatest ninja in all of Japan.

569
43:17.658 --> 43:22.079
Saizo hails from the same Iga clan.

570
43:24.456 --> 43:26.375
Hattori Hanzo…

571
43:29.253 --> 43:30.754
I'll kill him.

572
43:31.880 --> 43:32.965
The one who gave the order

573
43:34.007 --> 43:35.217
was Tokugawa Ieyasu.

574
43:36.552 --> 43:38.554
Then I'll kill them both!

575
43:51.525 --> 43:53.652
You came back with a companion.

576
43:56.530 --> 43:57.406
Sasuke.

577
43:58.157 --> 44:00.451
We share the same goal.

578
44:01.535 --> 44:02.578
What do you mean?

579
44:03.328 --> 44:06.707
We're after Ieyasu's head, too.

580
44:06.790 --> 44:10.169
My lord, we can't trust someone whose background we don't even know.

581
44:13.297 --> 44:14.548
Will you fight alongside us?

582
44:15.090 --> 44:16.550
Against the whole realm.

583
44:30.355 --> 44:31.940
Don't mess with me!

584
44:32.024 --> 44:34.276
Like hell I'll become your lackey.

585
44:34.359 --> 44:37.529
The old man died because of you.

586
44:37.613 --> 44:39.490
He chose the Sanada over the Tokugawa!

587
44:41.241 --> 44:43.285
That was a fine display of loyalty.

588
44:43.368 --> 44:45.204
What? Loyalty?

589
44:45.829 --> 44:47.581
To hell with that!

590
44:48.165 --> 44:50.125
That's enough, you bastard.

591
44:51.043 --> 44:52.836
I don't trust anyone.

592
44:56.757 --> 44:59.593
Will you put your skills to use for us?

593
45:08.810 --> 45:12.648
There was one piece missing, one we absolutely needed.

594
45:14.399 --> 45:15.275
And now,

595
45:16.068 --> 45:17.694
it falls right out of the sky.

596
45:19.154 --> 45:20.072
What?

597
45:23.116 --> 45:25.244
Damn, I'm bleeding too much.

598
45:26.620 --> 45:27.538
Oh, he fell.

599
45:31.458 --> 45:32.459
We've been spotted.

600
45:32.543 --> 45:34.294
Hey, isn't that bad?

601
45:35.337 --> 45:38.131
Could someone… bring him here?

602
45:42.010 --> 45:44.471
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone.

603
45:45.973 --> 45:47.099
We're leaving this village.

604
45:54.147 --> 45:56.775
We're taking down the Tokugawa.

605
46:29.057 --> 46:31.101
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

606
46:31.184 --> 46:34.021
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
